                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc>
                            <supportDesc>
                                <support>
                                    <p>Large rectangular block of grey limestone. Intact above, below and right, broken on the left. Finished rough on all sides. The left end is only broken at the front, so no further letters are formally missing from this block, but clearly another block is likely to have been attached to the left, at least. The left side is cut back sharply, from front to back, at an almost 45 degree angle; by contrast the right edge is perpendicular. There is some damaged to the upper surface at the right end, likely reflecting the original presence of a clamp.</p>
                                    <material type="inorganic.stone" subtype="unverified" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/66.html">limestone</material>
                                    <objectType ana="#object.block" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/189.html">block</objectType>
                                    <dimensions>
                                        <height unit="cm">35</height>
                                        <width unit="cm">85</width>
                                        <depth unit="cm">29</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                                <condition ana="#condition.fragment"/>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <p>Front face bears two lines of monumental letters, almost no spacing between the lines, with guidelines visible across the top of line 1.</p>
                                    <rs ana="#execution.chiselled" ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">chiselled</rs>
                                    <damage/>
                                </layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote>
                                <p>The letters are cut in a deep wide square cut, with a flat base to the cut, implying the inlay of some material originally; large triangular interpunct line 2.</p>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line1">Line 1</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="150" atMost="155">150-155</height>
                                </dimensions>
                                <locus from="line2" to="line2">Line 2</locus>
                                <dimensions type="letterHeight">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="140" atMost="150">140-150</height>
                                </dimensions>
                                <locus from="line1" to="line2">Interlineation line 1 to 2</locus>
                                <dimensions type="interlinear">
                                    <height unit="mm" atLeast="10" atMost="10">10</height>
                                </dimensions>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                    </physDesc>
